    "final_message": "Here's my recommendation for French cuisine open on Sunday in Paris:\n\n## 🍽️ Breizh Café\n\n| Detail | Information |\n|---|---|\n| **Cuisine** | French (Breton) |\n| **Rating** | ⭐ 3.9 |\n| **Address** | 109 Rue Vieille du Temple, 75003 Paris, France |\n| **Sunday Hours** | 9:00 AM – 11:00 PM |\n\n**Why this one:** Of the four French restaurants in Paris (Breizh Café, Le Baratin, Bistrot Paul Bert, and Chez L'Ami Jean), the other three are closed on Sundays — so Breizh Café is the only French option available on your arrival day, making it the best-rated choice for Sunday.\n\n**Guest review highlights:**\n- \"Best crepes in Paris, both sweet and savory\"\n- \"Authentic Breton cider and artisanal ingredients\"\n- \"Great ambiance and the staff is friendly\"\n- Gluten-free buckwheat crepes available\n- ⚠️ Heads-up: it's a busy spot, so expect a wait during peak hours\n\nWould you like me to make a reservation for Sunday, or check the other details like price per person and dietary options?",
